course: dictionary
lesson: 14949
title: A quick comeback
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A rejoinder is a quick reply that comes straight back at someone, usually in an argument or a chat. It is a formal word, so you will meet it more in books than in everyday talk. «"Tidy your room!" said Mum. "Tidy yours first!" was Sam's quick rejoinder.» Sam answers at once, straight back.
explain: A rejoinder is often clever, sharp or rude. Look at the words around it for clues about how it was said. «The sharp rejoinder made the whole class laugh» tells you it was clever enough to get a laugh.
explain: In stories you will find rejoinders in arguments and at parties. In Alice in Wonderland, Alice and the creatures trade rejoinders at the tea party, and in The Wind in the Willows Toad gives cheeky ones. When you meet one, ask yourself: who answered, and how sharp was the reply?
fact: A rejoinder is a quick reply, often given straight after someone else speaks.
fact: A rejoinder can be clever, sharp or rude.
fact: «Rejoinder» is a formal word, so it is most often found in books and writing.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, Alice and the creatures trade rejoinders at the tea party.
fact: A reply or an answer is close in meaning to rejoinder, but a rejoinder is usually quicker and sharper.
exercise: «"Tidy your room!" said Mum. "Tidy yours first!" was Sam's quick rejoinder.» What is a rejoinder? | A kind of meal | A long, sleepy story | A slow walk home | *A quick reply, often clever or sharp
exercise: Find the word in this sentence that means a quick, sharp reply: «The sharp rejoinder made the whole class laugh.» | *rejoinder | class | sharp | laugh
exercise: Why is rejoinder more often found in books than in chat? | *It is a formal word | It means something silly | It is a rude word | It is a baby word
test: In Alice in Wonderland, Alice and the creatures trade rejoinders at the tea party. What does trade rejoinders mean here? | Cook a meal together | Walk in a circle | *Swap quick, clever replies | Give away old toys
test: Mum tells Sam off, and Sam gives a rejoinder straight back. What is the best meaning of rejoinder? | A long letter | A nap | *A quick reply back | A hug
exam: «He ended the argument with a sharp rejoinder.» What does rejoinder mean in this sentence? | A quiet nap | A type of shoe | *A quick, sharp reply | A slow walk
